####################################################################
# cat1b_asystole_ibp.rq — CAT1b condition. HAND-AUTHORED.
#
# Answers CQ8 (manuscript Table 1): which clinical alarms coincide with alarms
# carrying a technical condition that reduces the validity of that sensing
# pathway?
#
# NL rule (CAT1): "If an asystole alarm occurs when an invasive blood
# pressure sensor is present without alarms on that sensing pathway, it may
# be flagged as likely false positive."
#
# Clause by clause (decisions agreed 2026-09-21, revised 2026-11-25):
#   "an asystole alarm"        — the arriving alarm's OWN metric is a
#                                cardiac rhythm (metric:CardiacRhythm or a
#                                kind of it) reported Absent or Fibrillation
#                                (or a refinement: VentricularFibrillation).
#                                Extended to fibrillation 2026-11-25, with
#                                the CardiacArrest criterion: a pulsatile,
#                                silent arterial line contradicts VF as much
#                                as asystole. NOT Philips' "VF or VT"
#                                (which cardiac_arrest.rq does count, for
#                                safety): a silent line does not contradict
#                                VT with a pulse, so flagging that alarm
#                                would hide a real VT (held, 2026-11-25).
#                                NOT VT or Abnormal. The metric is read
#                                from the alarm's own persistent graph (?gP:
#                                the metric no step consumes), its rhythm
#                                from its own transient graph (?gT). Never
#                                read from another alarm's graph: that let
#                                e.g. "Lage hartfreq." be flagged while an
#                                asystole was active. (Was metric:HeartRate
#                                until 2026-11-25; p99 annotates asystole on
#                                CardiacRhythm.)
#   "an invasive blood         — an ARTERIAL line on the IBP functional unit
#    pressure sensor"            of a PATIENT MONITOR (device:
#                                PhysiologicalMonitor or a subclass).
#                                Arterial = the line's pathway produces a
#                                metric that approximates
#                                physiologicalProperty:ArterialPressure
#                                (inference.ttl's restriction, as CAT2a reads
#                                it): ArterialBloodPressure and its phases.
#                                Recognised by what the line measures, not by
#                                the transducer's anatomical position, which
#                                the physiological ABP/ART blueprints do not
#                                state (2026-11-25). Deliberately narrower
#                                than the NL wording, which should read
#                                "invasive ARTERIAL blood pressure": ECMO
#                                circuit pressures (CARDIOHELP pArt/pVen,
#                                excluded by the device kind) and venous
#                                pressure do not show that the heart is
#                                beating — on VA-ECMO a real asystole
#                                coexists with a stable pressure.
#   "is present"               — observable only through the line's own
#                                alarms, and only through one whose pathway
#                                DELIVERED an arterial pressure (it carries
#                                the metric): its persistent graph (?gIbp,
#                                holding patient -> device -> functional unit
#                                -> transducer -> ... -> metric) remains in
#                                the store until 15 minutes after that alarm
#                                ended (ontology.ttl's
#                                postAlarmValidityDuration). An alarm
#                                without the metric ("ABP losgeraakt", "ART
#                                statische druk", "ABP artefact") shows a
#                                line exists but not that it works, and does
#                                not count. After 15 minutes of silence the
#                                line is no longer known to be there, and an
#                                asystole is not flagged — the safe error for
#                                a rule that downgrades one. Which pressure
#                                the evidence alarm reported (high or low) is
#                                deliberately not checked: what counts is that
#                                the line is silent NOW (agreed 2026-11-25).
#   "without alarms on that    — no current alarm on that IBP FUNCTIONAL
#    sensing pathway"            UNIT that breaks the premise (NOT EXISTS):
#                                checked per unit, not per transducer, so an
#                                active CVD or PAP alarm on the same monitor
#                                also blocks the flag (agreed 2026-11-25: the
#                                safe side). Every alarm on the unit breaks
#                                it UNLESS it reassures — shows a working
#                                arterial line delivering a pulsatile
#                                pressure (revised 2026-11-25, option A):
#                                its transducer is Arterial; it reports an
#                                INCREASED arterial pressure (Increased or a
#                                refinement, any phase) or ScalingError (the
#                                waveform exceeds the display scale); it
#                                reports nothing else (a sensor merely
#                                Enabled aside); and it is not itself
#                                flagged. A whitelist on purpose: any other
#                                or new state blocks, so annunciating is the
#                                default. NOT reassuring: a DECREASED
#                                pressure, mean or systolic/diastolic (a
#                                mean is computed from a flat curve too, and
#                                a falling pressure is what a real arrest
#                                produces within seconds); out of range
#                                (OutOfRange, OutOfLowRange, OutOfHighRange);
#                                quality problems; sensor faults; and every
#                                venous or pulmonary-artery alarm (a high
#                                venous pressure does not show cardiac
#                                output — it rises in an arrest).
#   "it may be flagged"        — flagged at onset, and WITHDRAWN if an alarm
#                                on that same IBP unit that breaks the
#                                premise (as above: any alarm that does not
#                                reassure) arrives while the asystole is
#                                still active: in a genuine asystole the
#                                pressure alarm follows the ECG alarm by
#                                seconds. See cat1b_withdraw.rq.
#
# FLAGGED ALARMS (agreed 2026-11-25, all rules): an alarm flagged likely
# false positive takes part in no other rule. An asystole CAT1a has already
# flagged (e.g. "ECG alle leads los" active) is not flagged a second time
# here. An IBP alarm flagged by CAT1a cannot serve as presence evidence
# while it is active (it then blocks the flag through NOT EXISTS, as does
# the technical alarm that caused its flag); once it has ended its flag is
# gone with its transient graph, so its persistent graph still counts as
# presence for the post-alarm window (OPEN, 2026-11-25).
#
# CONTRACT. Bound on entry: ?alarm (the arriving alarm), ?now.
# Binds: ?evidence (the IBP functional unit) and ?witness (the IBP alarm's
# persistent graph, hence the causing alarm).
# Used by actions/check.rq and actions/flag_insert.rq. The engine only
# evaluates it for alarms carrying a CardiacRhythm metric (a cheap gate;
# this condition decides).
#
# VALIDATION — engine/regression.py: cat1b_pos (arterial pressure alarm
# ended 10 min earlier), cat1b_other_monitor (arterial line on a Draeger
# monitor, a low-pressure alarm) and cat1b_range (a technical alarm that
# carries the arterial metric) flag; cat1b_neg (arterial line alarming
# now), cat1b_ecmo (ECMO circuit pressure only), cat1b_nometric (only a
# disconnect alarm on the line), cat1b_expired (evidence ended 20 min
# earlier), cat1b_venous (only a CVD line) and cat1b_unit (CVD alarm active
# on the same unit) do not; cat1b_withdraw is flagged and withdrawn when the
# arterial line alarms 8 s after onset; cat1b_vf (ventricular fibrillation,
# silent arterial line) flags; cat1b_vt (VT) and cat1b_vfvt (Philips "VF or
# VT") do not; cat1b_borrow flags the asystole but
# not a heart-rate alarm arriving during it; cat1b_flagged_incoming (an
# asystole already flagged by CAT1a is not flagged again).
####################################################################

PREFIX mda:                   <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX mdapoc:                <https://w3id.org/mda/poc#>
PREFIX rdf:                   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs:                  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl:                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX metric:                <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric/>
PREFIX rhythm:                <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric-rhythm/>
PREFIX functionalUnit:        <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/functional-unit/>
PREFIX device:                <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/device/>
PREFIX physiologicalProperty: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/physiological-property/>
PREFIX valuestate:            <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric-value-state/>
PREFIX qualitystate:          <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/quality-state/>
PREFIX opstate:               <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/operation-state/>
PREFIX position:              <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/anatomical-position/>

# an asystole or fibrillation alarm: its own metric is a cardiac rhythm,
# reported absent or fibrillating
GRAPH ?gT { ?alarm mda:hasMessage ?msg . ?msg mda:concernsPatient ?patient .
            ?metric mda:hasRhythm ?rhythm . }
?rhythm mda:refinesConcept* ?arrestRhythm .
VALUES ?arrestRhythm { rhythm:Absent rhythm:Fibrillation }
BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR(?alarm), "#persistent")) AS ?gP)
GRAPH ?gP { ?analysis mda:producesMetric ?metric . ?metric rdf:type ?metricType .
            FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?metric mda:analyzedBy ?nextStep } }
?metricType rdfs:subClassOf* metric:CardiacRhythm .
# not already flagged likely false positive (by CAT1a, which runs first)
FILTER NOT EXISTS { GRAPH ?gT { ?alarm mdapoc:flaggedLikelyFalsePositive ?earlierFlagEvidence } }
# an arterial line on a patient monitor, known present: an IBP alarm whose
# pathway delivered an arterial pressure, still in the store
GRAPH ?gIbp { ?patient mda:isMonitoredBy ?ibpDevice . ?ibpDevice rdf:type ?ibpDeviceType .
              ?ibpDevice mda:hasFunctionalUnit ?ibpFunctionalUnit .
              ?ibpFunctionalUnit rdf:type functionalUnit:FU_InvasiveBloodPressure .
              ?ibpStep mda:producesMetric ?ibpMetric . ?ibpMetric rdf:type ?ibpMetricType . }
?ibpDeviceType rdfs:subClassOf* device:PhysiologicalMonitor .
?ibpMetricType rdfs:subClassOf* ?arterialRestriction .
?arterialRestriction owl:onProperty mda:approximates ;
                     owl:hasValue physiologicalProperty:ArterialPressure .
# without a current alarm on that pathway (the IBP functional unit) that
# breaks the premise ...
FILTER NOT EXISTS {
  GRAPH ?gOther { ?other mda:hasMessage ?otherMsg . ?otherMsg mda:triggeredBy ?ibpDevice . }
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR(?other), "#persistent")) AS ?gOtherP)
  GRAPH ?gOtherP { ?ibpDevice mda:hasFunctionalUnit ?ibpFunctionalUnit . }
  # ... i.e. any such alarm, unless it REASSURES: it shows a working arterial
  # line delivering a pulsatile pressure (same block in cat1b_withdraw.rq)
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    GRAPH ?gOtherP { ?ibpFunctionalUnit mda:hasSensor ?okTransducer .
                     ?okTransducer mda:hasAnatomicalPosition position:Arterial . }
    { GRAPH ?gOther { ?okMetric mda:hasValueState ?okValue . }
      ?okValue mda:refinesConcept* valuestate:Increased .
      GRAPH ?gOtherP { ?okMetric rdf:type ?okMetricType . }
      ?okMetricType rdfs:subClassOf* ?okRestriction .
      ?okRestriction owl:onProperty mda:approximates ;
                     owl:hasValue physiologicalProperty:ArterialPressure . }
    UNION
    { GRAPH ?gOther { ?okSignal mda:hasQualityState qualitystate:ScalingError . } }
    # and it reports nothing else (a sensor merely Enabled aside)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      GRAPH ?gOther { ?anyNode ?anyStateProp ?anyState . }
      VALUES ?anyStateProp { mda:hasValueState mda:hasRhythm mda:hasQualityState
                             mda:hasSensorOperationState mda:hasComponentOperationState
                             mda:hasDeviceOperationState }
      FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?anyState mda:refinesConcept* valuestate:Increased }
      FILTER(?anyState NOT IN (qualitystate:ScalingError, opstate:Enabled))
    }
    # and it is not itself flagged likely false positive
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { GRAPH ?gOther { ?other mdapoc:flaggedLikelyFalsePositive ?okFlag } }
  }
}
BIND(?ibpFunctionalUnit AS ?evidence)
BIND(?gIbp AS ?witness)
